From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH kbase-common 002] kmod: compile kbase_kmod.c when kbase KMD
 selected

Purpose: Build the Kbase backend into libpankmod when
 -Dpanfrost-kmds includes kbase. Keeps upstream panfrost+panthor files
 unconditional (unlike the G720 reference, which gates them too — we do
 not take that behavioral change).
Source/Reference: https://github.com/wonderkast02/panvk-g720-kbase-csf
 branch android-candidate-beta-1.9.4
 (src/panfrost/lib/kmod/meson.build), adapted: upstream file list kept,
 only the kbase conditional appended.
Tested GPU: none yet (build plumbing only).
Tested Kbase UAPI: n/a.
Mesa base range: 26.3.0-devel (pinned 5a07217f034b3e50d8c7c7794f97a2df1742613b).
Dependencies: 001-meson-kmds-option.patch (panfrost_kmds variable).
Validation test: meson setup + ninja build of pankmod_lib with kbase.

diff --git a/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/meson.build b/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/meson.build
--- a/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/meson.build
+++ b/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/meson.build
@@ -6,6 +6,10 @@
   'panfrost_kmod.c',
   'panthor_kmod.c',
 )
+
+if panfrost_kmds.contains('kbase')
+  libpankmod_lib_files += files('kbase_kmod.c')
+endif

 libpankmod_lib = static_library(
   'pankmod_lib',
